<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../partials/head') %></head>
<body>
<div class="app">
<%- include('../partials/sidebar') %>
<%- include('../partials/topbar') %>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="hint mt-0">
        <strong>Keyword research says what people ask an assistant. This says who the assistant can answer
        them from.</strong> A grounded assistant — ChatGPT search, Copilot, Perplexity — answers a question by
        running its own search first and reading the pages that come back. That result set is the population
        every citation is drawn from, so this report samples it for each question and reports whether this
        site is in it.
      </p>
      <p class="hint">
        <strong>What this is, said precisely.</strong> Being in the pool means an assistant <em>could</em> quote
        the page — necessary, not sufficient. Being absent from it means no citation is possible for that
        question today, which is the finding worth acting on. That asymmetry is the value here; a percentage
        labelled "citation rate" would not be.
      </p>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <strong>What it is not.</strong> It is not a measurement of citations actually made. No keyless endpoint
        reports what ChatGPT, Gemini or Perplexity cited, and this deployment holds no citation-tracking
        credential — so that number is not knowable here and nothing on this page estimates it. For proof of
        real citations, read <a href="/ai-seo/ai-referrals">AI referral traffic</a>: a session arriving from an
        assistant is a person who read an answer and clicked the link in it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%- include('_partials/brandpicker') %>

  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head"><h3>Check who gets cited</h3></div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <% if (brand && !derivedPrompts.length) { %>
            <p class="hint" style="color:var(--critical,#b91c1c)">
              <strong>No questions are available for this brand yet.</strong>
              <% if (!researchRun) { %>
                Nothing has been produced by <a href="/ai-seo/research?brand=<%= brand.id %>">keyword
                research</a> for it. Run that first — its assistant prompts and question-shaped keywords are
                picked up here automatically — or paste a list below.
              <% } else { %>
                The last research run produced no assistant prompts and no question-shaped keywords. That
                happens when AI assistance was switched off for the run (the prompt half needs the model) and
                the keyword set contained no questions. Paste a list below, or re-run research with AI on.
              <% } %>
            </p>
          <% } %>

          <form method="POST" action="/ai-seo/answer-citations/run"><%- csrfField %>
            <% if (brand) { %><input type="hidden" name="brand_id" value="<%= brand.id %>"><% } %>

            <div class="field">
              <label for="prompts">Questions to check
                <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-3)">(one per line — leave empty to use the
                <%= derivedPrompts.length %> from the last research run)</span>
              </label>
              <textarea id="prompts" name="prompts" rows="6"
                placeholder="how long does iso 27001 certification take&#10;what is the difference between iso 27001 and soc 2&#10;is a cissp worth it for a cloud engineer"></textarea>
              <p class="hint mt-0" style="margin-bottom:0">
                Whole questions, not keywords. The sample is taken on the question as written, because that is
                what an assistant's own grounding search runs on. Lines shorter than 12 characters are ignored.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="field">
              <label for="country">Market</label>
              <select id="country" name="country">
                <% marketList.forEach(function (m) { %>
                  <option value="<%= m.code %>" <%= m.code === selectedMarket ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= m.label %></option>
                <% }) %>
              </select>
            </div>

            <div class="field">
              <label for="per_prompt">Pool depth per question</label>
              <select id="per_prompt" name="per_prompt">
                <option value="5">Top 5</option>
                <option value="10" selected>Top 10</option>
                <option value="20">Top 20</option>
              </select>
              <p class="hint mt-0" style="margin-bottom:0">
                Ten matches what a grounded assistant typically reads before answering. Twenty finds more
                near-misses but takes longer and tells you less about what would actually be quoted.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="field">
              <label for="limit">Maximum questions this run</label>
              <input type="number" id="limit" name="limit" min="1" max="<%= maxPrompts %>" value="<%= maxPrompts %>">
              <p class="hint mt-0" style="margin-bottom:0">
                Each question is one paced request against an endpoint that rate-limits, so they run one at a
                time with a gap. <%= maxPrompts %> questions is roughly two to three minutes.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="btn-row">
              <button type="submit" class="btn" <%= perms.canWrite && brand ? '' : 'disabled' %>>Check the retrieval pool</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>

      <% if (competitorDomains.length) { %>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><h3>Compared against</h3></div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="mt-0">
              <% competitorDomains.forEach(function (d) { %><span class="chip"><%= d %></span><% }) %>
            </p>
            <p class="hint" style="margin-bottom:0">
              The brand's named competitors, from <a href="/ai-seo/competitors<%= brand ? '?brand=' + brand.id : '' %>">competitive
              intelligence</a>. A question where one of these is in the pool and this site is not becomes a gap
              row — the actionable half of the report. Discovered competitors are deliberately not used: an
              auto-built list fills the table with directories and aggregators nobody is trying to outrank.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } else if (brand) { %>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="hint mt-0" style="margin-bottom:0">
              <strong>No competitors are named for this brand.</strong> The run still works — it reports pool
              presence and the domains that occupy it — but the gap list needs named competitors to separate
              "a rival can be quoted here and we cannot" from "nobody strong answers this". Add them on
              <a href="/ai-seo/competitors<%= '?brand=' + brand.id %>">competitive intelligence</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <div>
      <% if (derivedPrompts.length) { %>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <h3>Questions from the last research run</h3>
            <span class="muted" style="font-size:12px"><%= derivedPrompts.length %> found</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="hint mt-0">
              Used automatically when the box on the left is empty. From
              <a href="/ai-seo/research/<%= researchRun.id %>">research run #<%= researchRun.id %></a>,
              finished <%= fmtDate(researchRun.finished_at) %>.
            </p>
            <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data compact">
              <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Source</th><th>Job</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
              <% derivedPrompts.forEach(function (p) { %>
                <tr>
                  <td><%= p.prompt %></td>
                  <td>
                    <span class="badge <%= p.origin === 'assistant-prompt' ? 'accent' : 'neutral' %>">
                      <%= p.origin === 'assistant-prompt' ? 'assistant prompt' : 'search question' %>
                    </span>
                  </td>
                  <td class="muted" style="font-size:12px"><%= p.job || '—' %></td>
                </tr>
              <% }) %>
              </tbody>
            </table></div>
            <p class="hint" style="margin-bottom:0">
              <strong>Two origins, and the difference matters.</strong> An <em>assistant prompt</em> is a whole
              question with a stated situation, written by the model because it cannot be derived from a keyword
              list. A <em>search question</em> is a question-shaped query this site already earns impressions
              for — smaller, but observed rather than generated.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%- include('_partials/runs') %>

<%- include('../partials/sidebar-end') %>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
